  "description": "The proposal seeks to retain the basement as non‑habitable ancillary space while undertaking excavation works to increase the floor‑to‑ceiling height to approximately 2.3 metres. The works include digging down and underpinning the existing foundations to achieve the required headroom and ensure structural stability.\n\nThe renovated basement will accommodate ancillary uses only, including a utility room, gym/exercise area, and general storage. As part of the works, a new waterproofing system will be installed to provide a dry and structurally protected environment in accordance with current best‑practice basement construction standards.\n\nThe proposal also includes the formation of a new lightwell to improve natural light and ventilation to the basement level. No changes are proposed to the building’s external appearance other than the addition of the lightwell, and the works do not create any new habitable rooms.",
